An OTP `onPaste` handler calls `e.preventDefault()` and then this helper. The first box already holds `9`, and the user pastes `12 34-567` into the second box (index 1). What does the helper return?

```js
function applyPaste(digits, start, text) {
  const chars = text.replace(/\D/g, '').split('');
  const next = [...digits];
  chars.forEach((c, k) => {
    if (start + k < next.length) next[start + k] = c;
  });
  const focus = Math.min(start + chars.length, next.length - 1);
  return { next, focus };
}
applyPaste(['9', '', '', '', '', ''], 1, '12 34-567');
```

`App` owns `user` and `logout`. `Layout` and `Sidebar` only forward them to `UserMenu`. Which refactor removes the drilling **without** Context and keeps a single source of truth?

```jsx
function App() {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
  const logout = () => setUser(null);
  return <Layout user={user} onLogout={logout} />;
