Callers use your hook as `useFetch('/api/items', { headers: { Accept: 'application/json' } })`. With `[url, options]` as dependencies, it refetches in an endless loop. Which change **inside the hook** stops the loop but still refetches when the headers really change?

```jsx
function useFetch(url, options) {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch(url, options).then(r => r.json()).then(setData);
  }, [url, options]);
  return data;
}
```

A candidate writes this debounce. What does the snippet log?

