A timer formats seconds as HH:MM:SS with this function. What does `format(3725)` return?

```js
function format(totalSeconds) {
  const h = Math.floor(totalSeconds / 3600);
  const m = Math.floor(totalSeconds / 60);
  const s = totalSeconds % 60;
  return [h, m, s].map(n => String(n).padStart(2, '0')).join(':');
}
```

A currency converter keeps both fields in state and syncs them with two effects. The rate is 83.17 INR per USD. Both fields start at 0, and the user types `1` into the INR field. What does the INR field end up showing?

```jsx
const round2 = n => Math.round(n * 100) / 100;
const [inr, setInr] = useState(0);
const [usd, setUsd] = useState(0);
useEffect(() => { setUsd(round2(inr / 83.17)); }, [inr]);
useEffect(() => { setInr(round2(usd * 83.17)); }, [usd]);
// inputs: value={inr} onChange → setInr(Number(e.target.value)), same for usd
```

